candle-audio-mmaudio is an independent, from-scratch Rust/candle reimplementation
of the MMAudio video-to-audio architecture — the MM-DiT flow-matching generator,
the DFN5B-CLIP and Synchformer conditioning encoders, both mel-VAE stages, and
the 16 kHz BigVGAN / 44.1 kHz BigVGAN v2 vocoders. It does not include or
redistribute any model weights.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored third-party source (NOT shipped)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

One frozen third-party reference implementation IS redistributed with this
crate, under `_vendor/`. It is a dev-only parity oracle: it is Python, it is
never imported by any Rust crate, and it is not part of any shipped bundle.

  * MMAudio reference       https://github.com/hkchengrex/MMAudio       (MIT)
    `_vendor/mmaudio/` — verbatim copy of the `mmaudio/` package at commit
    974010a026c731054592d8f777218bd9d85a6c24, redistributed under the MIT
    license reproduced at `_vendor/mmaudio/LICENSE`.
    Copyright (c) 2024 Sony Research Inc. The package carries three further
    upstream notices for code it embeds, all vendored alongside it:
    `ext/bigvgan/LICENSE` and `ext/bigvgan_v2/LICENSE` (NVIDIA BigVGAN, MIT,
    each with an `incl_licenses/` directory of its own dependencies' notices)
    and `ext/synchformer/LICENSE` (Synchformer). See `_vendor/VENDORED.md` for
    provenance, the pinned producer environment, and what was excluded.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived third-party goldens (test fixtures, NOT shipped)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Five parity tests are gated by committed "golden" fixtures: numbers produced by
running the vendored reference above, once, against the pinned model weights and
freezing the result. They are dev-only — they live under `tests/fixtures/`, are
read only by `#[test]` code, and are not part of any shipped bundle.

  * `tests/fixtures/mmaudio_parity_*.safetensors` (sc-17285)
    Generated by `scripts/reference/mmaudio_reference.py dump`, which records
    the producing snapshot revisions and environment in
    `tests/fixtures/mmaudio_parity_metadata.json`. Consumed by
    `parity_reference.rs`, `parity_reference_44k.rs`,
    `parity_reference_44k_decoder.rs`, `conformance_output.rs` and
    `mmdit_conformance.rs`.

    These fixtures contain no third-party source and no model weights: they are
    conditioning features, latents, mel spectrograms and waveforms — numerical
    output of the models named below, over a synthetic clip and prompt authored
    in this repository. The clip is generated in closed form by
    `mmaudio_reference.py` and carries no footage licence of its own.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights (NOT distributed with this crate)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model weights are supplied by the caller. Neither this crate nor its tests
download them: inference never self-fetches and never derives a hub-cache
location (epic 13657). They remain subject to the licenses of their respective
providers, recorded per component in `release/real-weight-models.toml`:

  * MMAudio MM-DiT (small_16k, large_44k_v2) and both mel-VAEs (v1-16, v1-44),
    plus the 16 kHz BigVGAN — hkchengrex/MMAudio, CC-BY-NC-4.0
    (non-commercial).
  * DFN5B-CLIP-ViT-H-14-378 — apple/DFN5B-CLIP-ViT-H-14-378, under the Apple
    Machine Learning Research Model License. MMAudio supplies 384×384 inputs to this 378-native
    checkpoint; both resolutions produce the same 27×27 patch grid with its patch-14 convolution.
  * Synchformer — hkchengrex/MMAudio, MIT.
  * BigVGAN v2 44 kHz — nvidia/bigvgan_v2_44khz_128band_512x, MIT.

The MMAudio DiT/VAE and DFN5B-CLIP weights are research / non-commercial;
SceneWorks is non-commercial and surfaces these licenses to the user
(epic-12833 decision), which is what makes running them in the real-weight
regression guard in-policy.

